msgstr "![The Jordan-Wigner transpiled LUCJ circuit.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/lucj-7.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This pipeline is exactly what [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") assembles, so reach for the preset in practice and build the stages by hand when you need to change one of them:\n"
msgstr "Esse pipeline é exatamente o que [`generate_preset_jw_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-jw-pass-manager#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_jw_pass_manager\") monta, então na prática use o preset e construa as etapas manualmente quando precisar alterar alguma delas:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"match-the-device-topology\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Match the device topology {#5-match-the-device-topology}"
msgstr "5. Ajuste à topologia do dispositivo {#5-match-the-device-topology}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A real device has a restricted qubit coupling map, and the LUCJ ansatz is designed to match it. The same-spin (`pairs_aa`) interactions form two linear chains and the alpha-beta (`pairs_ab`) interactions bridge them. ffsim’s [`generate_lucj_pass_manager()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.qiskit.generate_lucj_pass_manager.html#ffsim.qiskit.generate_lucj_pass_manager \"(in ffsim)\") builds a device-aware qubit pipeline for this structure, and returns the subset of `pairs_ab` the hardware can actually accommodate. Slot that pipeline into the preset’s `qubit` stage while keeping the package’s own fermion-to-qubit synthesis:\n"
msgstr "Um dispositivo real tem um mapa de acoplamento de qubits restrito, e o ansatz LUCJ foi projetado para se ajustar a ele. As interações de mesmo spin (`pairs_aa`) formam duas cadeias lineares e as interações alfa-beta (`pairs_ab`) fazem a ponte entre elas. O [`generate_lucj_pass_manager()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.qiskit.generate_lucj_pass_manager.html#ffsim.qiskit.generate_lucj_pass_manager \"(in ffsim)\") do ffsim constrói um pipeline de qubits ciente do dispositivo para essa estrutura, e retorna o subconjunto de `pairs_ab` que o hardware consegue de fato acomodar. Encaixe esse pipeline na etapa `qubit` do preset, mantendo a síntese férmion-para-qubit própria do pacote:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That composition is the point: the `qubit` stage is device-aware, while the fermion-to-qubit synthesis stage ahead of it stays this package’s own, and so stays replaceable. Replacing the `qubit` stage does drop what the preset registers there, which is the [`HopEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-hop-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.HopEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.HopEvolutionSynthesis\") that turns the Givens factors of an orbital rotation into [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate)objects. Pass it on through the `hls_config` as above, or the device’s basis has to be reached without it.\n"
msgstr "Essa composição é o ponto central: a etapa `qubit` é ciente do dispositivo, enquanto a etapa de síntese férmion-para-qubit que vem antes continua sendo a do próprio pacote e, portanto, continua substituível. Substituir a etapa `qubit` descarta o que o preset registra ali, que é o [`HopEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-hop-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.HopEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.HopEvolutionSynthesis\") que transforma os fatores de Givens de uma rotação de orbitais em objetos [`XXPlusYYGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XXPlusYYGate)Passe-o adiante pelo `hls_config` como acima, ou a base do dispositivo precisará ser alcançada sem ele.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With `pm.qubit` now set to the device-aware pipeline, running the pass manager lays the circuit out on the backend’s qubits and routes it to the coupling map. For the *unrestricted* ansatz from step 1, whose diagonal Coulomb operator still contains alpha-beta terms the hardware cannot reach directly, the router must insert many `SWAP` gates to bridge them:\n"
msgstr "Com `pm.qubit` agora definido como o pipeline ciente do dispositivo, executar o pass manager posiciona o circuito nos qubits do backend e o roteia para o mapa de acoplamento. Para o ansatz *irrestrito* do passo 1, cujo operador de Coulomb diagonal ainda contém termos alfa-beta que o hardware não consegue alcançar diretamente, o roteador precisa inserir muitas portas `SWAP` para fazer a ponte:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Restrict the ansatz to the hardware-implementable interactions**\n"
msgstr "**Restrinja o ansatz às interações implementáveis no hardware**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The fix is to feed `allowed_pairs_ab` back into the ansatz construction, through the `interaction_pairs` argument of [`from_t_amplitudes()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.html#ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.from_t_amplitudes \"(in ffsim)\"), so the diagonal Coulomb operator only contains alpha-beta terms the coupling map can implement directly. The ansatz then matches the device topology and the router barely has to touch it:\n"
msgstr "A solução é realimentar `allowed_pairs_ab` na construção do ansatz, por meio do argumento `interaction_pairs` de [`from_t_amplitudes()`](https://qiskit-community.github.io/ffsim/api/stubs/ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.html#ffsim.UCJOpSpinBalanced.from_t_amplitudes \"(in ffsim)\"), de modo que o operador de Coulomb diagonal contenha apenas termos alfa-beta que o mapa de acoplamento consegue implementar diretamente. O ansatz então se ajusta à topologia do dispositivo e o roteador quase não precisa mexer nele:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Drawing only the active qubits (`idle_wires=False`) shows the circuit restricted to the two spin chains and the alpha-beta bridge, expressed in the device basis gates. Layout and routing scatter the logical modes across the device’s physical qubits, so pass a `wire_order` taken from the circuit’s final layout ([`final_index_layout()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.TranspileLayout#final_index_layout) lists the physical qubit each input qubit ended on, in input-qubit order) to draw the wires back in the original mode order:\n"
msgstr "Desenhar apenas os qubits ativos (`idle_wires=False`) mostra o circuito restrito às duas cadeias de spin e à ponte alfa-beta, expresso nas portas de base do dispositivo. O layout e o roteamento espalham os modos lógicos pelos qubits físicos do dispositivo, então passe um `wire_order` tirado do layout final do circuito ([`final_index_layout()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.TranspileLayout#final_index_layout) lista o qubit físico em que cada qubit de entrada terminou, na ordem dos qubits de entrada) para desenhar os fios de volta na ordem original dos modos:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The hardware-restricted LUCJ circuit routed onto the heavy-hex device coupling map.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/lucj-12.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The hardware-restricted LUCJ circuit routed onto the heavy-hex device coupling map.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/lucj-12.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The exact post-layout gate counts and depth depend on the routing/optimization passes and the chosen device, so they are not reproduced here. The key point is the co-design; expressing the ansatz with a nearest-neighbor `pairs_aa` chain and hardware-filtered `pairs_ab` bridges keeps the synthesized circuit close to the device topology, minimizing the routing overhead (inserted `SWAP` gates). See [`FermionicSlaterGivensDecomposition`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-slater-givens-decomposition#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSlaterGivensDecomposition \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSlaterGivensDecomposition\") for a related synthesis choice (`minimize_2q_gate_count`), trading two-qubit gate count against routed depth.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  As contagens exatas de portas e a profundidade após o layout dependem das passagens de roteamento/otimização e do dispositivo escolhido, por isso não são reproduzidas aqui. O ponto principal é o co-design; expressar o ansatz com uma cadeia `pairs_aa` de vizinhos mais próximos e pontes `pairs_ab` filtradas pelo hardware mantém o circuito sintetizado próximo da topologia do dispositivo, minimizando a sobrecarga de roteamento (portas `SWAP` inseridas). Veja [`FermionicSlaterGivensDecomposition`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-slater-givens-decomposition#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSlaterGivensDecomposition \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSlaterGivensDecomposition\") para uma escolha de síntese relacionada (`minimize_2q_gate_count`), que troca a contagem de portas de dois qubits pela profundidade roteada.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

